:: OC Tyler Intro [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $OCTylerSocial to 0>>
<<set $OCTylerSocialRank to 0>>
You are walking along the path near the swing sets when you hear two sounds. <span style="color:Yellow">The first is a cry of distress while the other is amused laughter. This combination can only mean one thing in a middle school full of young boys. Someone is getting bullied.</span> You peer over towards one set of swings to find the usual suspects, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> and his crowd of goons surrounding an unfamiliar boy on the ground in a fetal position. <span style="color:Yellow">Seems he’s the victim for today.</span> 

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Michael",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Uniform",
                Mouth: "Smirk",
                Eyes: "Tired",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "OC Tyler",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Uniform",
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Eyes: "Sad",
                Blush: 1,
                Cry: 1,
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Come on! Say something again!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> laughs, <span style="color:Yellow">kicking dirt at the boy,</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Oi! Fancy some tea? Pip pip cherry-o! Been here 8 months and that accent still sounds as stupid as ever. Learn to talk like a normal person.”</span> He is giving a poor, over-the-top attempt at a British accent as some of the other kids join in, saying the most stereotypical English things in accents so bad it makes your head hurt. <span style="color:Yellow">The kid on the ground doesn’t move or say anything, continuing to lie there covering his head probably hoping they’ll all just leave him alone.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“What’s wrong?”</span> The biggest of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>’s goons ask, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Weren’t you just swinging a stick around pretending to be some warrior? Well, now’s the time to prove yourself! Or are you just tough in those stupid make-believe games you play? Only babies play pretend!”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Actually, tabletop role playing games are pretty popular with adults and-”</span> The small, glasses wearing goon begins to say until everyone looks at him with a weird expression. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Ye- yeah! I mean, Dungeons and Dorks, am I right?”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Can I give him a wedgie for saying that?”</span> The dumb goon asks <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“You know what, that’s not a bad idea!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> smirks. The small goon looks afraid for a second, <span style="color:Pink">until <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> reaches down and grips the fetal boy’s underwear instead! He yanks on his red and blue briefs, causing the boy to straighten out and cry in pain as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> doesn’t hold back.</span> It is at this point that you realize the boy is wearing a red face mask. A bit odd, but it does little to muffle his pained cries as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> lifts him off the ground by his underwear. <span style="color:LightCoral">You doubt <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> and his goons will leave him alone until the bell rings and doubt even more that anyone else will come to his aid.</span> <br>
<br>
<div id="choice">
	<<link "Step in<br>">>
	<<replace "#choice">>
        <span style="color:LightGreen">You gather up all of your courage and strength, straightening your back to try and appear taller, and call out for <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> and his goons to leave that kid alone!</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> pauses and turns to you, still holding the poor boy about a foot off the ground by his briefs, and smirks. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Oh? Or what? Are you going to stop us?”</span> <span style="color:LightCoral"> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>’s goons all turn to you with smiles, making it clear just how outnumbered you are. <br>
        <br>
        You gulp, trying not to sound afraid as you repeat yourself.</span> Leave that kid alone, or else. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> drops the boy, causing him to faceplant into the dirt, and happily begins to stroll over. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“You know what, boys? I think the school could use some more decorations. What do you say we strip our volunteers here down and tie them to the front gates by their cocks? May not be much to work with, but we’ll make do.”</span> <span style="color:LightCoral">They all smile deviously as they approach you.</span> 
            
        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Michael",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Uniform",
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                    Eyes: "Tired",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Eyes: "Mad",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "OC Tyler",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Uniform",
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Eyes: "Sad",
                    Blush: 1,
                    Cry: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

        You take a step back, <span style="color:LightCoral">nervous that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>’s idea doesn’t seem like just an idle threat.</span> You think about running, crying for help, or maybe even trying to fight them off. <span style="color:LightGreen">But thankfully, someone up there seems to be looking out for you as one of his goons suddenly taps <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> on the shoulders and points off to the side. You all turn at once and see a teacher walk out of the cafeteria and sit down on a nearby bench with a book.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Shit.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> sighs, cursing under his breath, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“You got lucky this time. But next time you want to try and play hero, that cock becomes a leash. Let’s go!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> and his goons walk off, sticking their tongues out at you and making obscene gestures. <span style="color:LightGreen">Once they are out of sight, you run over to the boy and check if he’s okay.</span> <br>
        <<socialChange "Michael" -3>>
        <br>
        <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Oww… are- are they gone?”</span> He says in a thick British accent, as you expected. <span style="color:Pink">He sticks his hands into the front of his bottoms to fix his wedgie.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Tha- thanks… I thought they were going to hang me from the swings.”</span> The boy avoids eye contact with you, staring at the ground with slightly flushed cheeks under his mask. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“My- my name is <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Tyler</span>.”</span> You smile and introduce yourself to the boy, shaking his hand. <br>
        <br>
        <<include"OC Tyler Intro 2">>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
	<<link "Walk Away<br>">>
	<<replace "#choice">>
        As bad as you feel for the kid, <span style="color:Pink">the poor lad now being lifted onto the swings by his briefs,</span> you don’t think you can do anything to help him. Sadly, a wedgie or two just comes with the territory of growing up. <span style="color:Yellow">The worst thing he’ll get is some sore balls.</span> <br>
        <br>
        So, you walk away, leaving him to his fate as his pained cries fade into the distance. <span style="color:Yellow">Odds are, with how easy a target he is making himself, you’ll see this exact situation play out again in the future.</span> <br>
        <<addMoodlet "Stress" 0>>
        <<needChange "Fun" 20>>
