    <<if $MichaelSocial >= 50 or $MichaelSocialRank > 0>>
        <<link "Tell Michael to Stop<br>">>
        <<replace "#choice">>
            You sigh, knowing <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> is a bully but feel your friend may be going too far. Either he’s going to get himself in trouble or hurt the kid, neither you want to see right now, so you call out to him. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Oh, hey <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$MichaelNickname</span>!”</span> He laughs, waving you over, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Want a shot at this? This dork was swinging some stick around playing pretend or some shit. Oh, you should hear him talk! Sounds like those fancy people on T.V.!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> goes to kick dirt at him again, trying to get him to speak, when you stop him. <span style="color:Yellow">You tell him the kid's had enough, so they should leave him alone.</span>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Michael",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: "Uniform",
                        Mouth: "Smirk",
                        Eyes: "Tired",
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Eyes: "Tired",
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "OC Tyler",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: "Uniform",
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Eyes: "Sad",
                        Blush: 1,
                        Cry: 1,
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

            <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Oh, come on! You’re no fun! We’re just messing around!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> scoffs at you, but you persist. You point out how he doesn’t have the best reputation with teachers and there are plenty around today. If they see him and his goons surrounding the poor kid, they’ll probably assume the worst and give him a week’s detention. Is this really worth a week of getting his ass reddened by Randolph? <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> <span style="color:Pink">blushes at this, his goons turning to him nervously.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Alright, alright. Point made. God, you’re such a buzzkill. Come on guys, let’s leave Mr. Tea & Crumpets here to play his stupid game of pretend.”</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">They all walk off, leaving you and the boy alone.</span> <br>
            <br>
            He stands up, fixing his wedgie and giving you a nervous and unsure look. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Tha… thanks?”</span> <span style="color:Yellow">He takes a step back, obviously not sure if you are a friend or foe based on how chummy you were with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>.</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">You smile and assure him you’re not here to bully him or anything.</span> You also apologize on <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>’s behalf, he can be a real jerk sometimes, but isn’t that bad… well, he isn’t COMPLETELY bad… most of the time. <br>
            <br>
            <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I… ummm…”</span> The boy looks down nervously, fiddling with his fingers. You try to lighten the mood by introducing yourself and holding out your hand. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Oh- I- I’m <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Tyler</span>!”</span> He shakes your hand, his British accent just as thick as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> claimed. <span style="color:Pink">It’s kind of cute to hear such a young voice speak with such an accent.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Tha- thanks again…”</span><br>
            <br>
            <<include"OC Tyler Intro 2">>
        <</replace>>
        <</link>>
    <</if>>
</div>

:: OC Tyler Intro 2 [nobr]

/* Intro */
The boy continues to stare at the ground awkwardly, kicking away a small rock. He glances up at you once, but as soon as your eyes meet, he quickly turns away turning even redder. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I… D- do you… chocolate bar…”</span> You hear him mumble very quietly. You raise an eyebrow, asking him to repeat himself louder. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I- I- I have a chocolate bar.”</span> He points to his backpack nearby, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Do- do you want half? For… for helping me?”</span> <span style="color:Pink">He tries to give you a smile, but quickly blushes once more, turning around and covering his face. The boy sure is shy. You nod; you’d love to split a candy bar with him.</span>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "OC Tyler",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Uniform",
                Mouth: "Happy",
                Eyes: "Sad",
                Blush: 1,
                Cry: 1,
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Tyler</span> walks over and pulls a decent-sized bar out of his bag and breaks it in half, <span style="color:LightGreen">notably giving you the larger half, before you both sit on the swings to enjoy it.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“S- sorry. I’m not good with new people.”</span> He says softly, trying to explain his quiet and stuttering speak. You tell him it’s fine, <span style="color:Pink">smiling and finally getting the boy to look at you for a second without turning away.</span> <br>
<br>
You ask him about himself and, though he seems very nervous about sharing, he explains that he moved here near the end of the last school year, just missing the cut-off point for Preston. That explains the thick accent. <br>
<br>

<<if $Player.Traits.includes("Nerd")>>
    When asked about his interests, he shyly explains that he enjoys video games, especially RPGs. <span style="color:LightGreen">At the mention of TTRPGs, you smile. You explain that you’re a bit of a nerd yourself and have played a few tabletop RPGs in your day. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Tyler</span> seems to light up at this, snapping his head up and quickly asking what kind you’ve played and what sort of characters you’ve made.</span> Though he quickly gets shy again once he realizes how over-excited he sounded. <span style="color:Pink">You laugh it off, it was kind of cute, and the two of you enjoy your time together before you part ways.</span> <br>
    <<addMoodlet "Stress" 0>>
    <<needChange "Fun" 20>>
    <<socialChange "Tyler" 5 1>>
    <<set $CompletedQuests.push("Tyler: Introduction")>>
    <<set $InActiveQuests.delete("Tyler: Introduction")>>
    <br>
    [[Continue|School Courtyard]]
<<else>>
    He seems a bit nervous about telling you his interests, which are as you expected. Video Games, RPGs, and other very nerdy activities. Not uncommon for a boy his age. <span style="color:LightGreen">He seems a bit more at ease when you don’t instantly start making fun of him and the two of you enjoy a nice conversation before you part ways.</span> <br>
    <<addMoodlet "Stress" 0>>
    <<needChange "Fun" 20>>
    <<socialChange "Tyler" 3 1>>
    <<set $CompletedQuests.push("Tyler: Introduction")>>
    <<set $InActiveQuests.delete("Tyler: Introduction")>>
